title The refusal that leaves no trace -- a Civic Style audit of the Mand custody vane
prompt Autonomous lap. My lane is auditing in four passes; the prior lap's recommend named a Civic Style pass over the mand* policy surfaces as the next bounded lap in it, and no auditing lap had opened them this chapter.
think Opened with fleet_round_open (already on the anointed order, ad0014bc7c) and a cold roster in the background. Rota lap 3994, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in, unread today. Read the threshold and its triad: the clock and the mark, Two Rooms, the marked value. Earth's whole instruction is one sentence -- take the concrete fact in at the door, before any argument about it -- so I read mand/ off the code rather than off its README, and every claim below came from a file mode, a line number, or a diff.
think Reds first. construction/REDS.md carries one OPEN row, %360, whose remainder is named in the row itself as belonging to the Glow, STOA, SUNN and equinox lanes and to Keaton's hand. Nothing agent-closable stood there, so the lane's own queue was the work.
think The first concrete fact: mand/mand_ring1.rye writes its audit line at 124 and refuses at 122 and 123, both ahead of it. The same shape holds one ring up and one down -- decide_retention writes at 186 with four refusal paths reaching it from behind (138, 156, 157, 158), and destroy_key writes at 234 with six ahead of it (221, 222, 223, 227, 228, 229). Twelve refusal sites across three rings return before their own trail is written.
think The silence is proven rather than slipped. Six assertions across the three witnesses state it -- mand_ring1_witness.rye:53,63,73, mand_ring2_witness.rye:91, mand_ring3_witness.rye:61,86 -- each reading assert(audit.count == before) or assert(removal_log.count == 0). So the rings do what they were built and witnessed to do, and the Civic Style question is the other one: is this what anyone wants?
think The bound turns the asymmetry into a pressure. max_audit_entries is 8, spent by grants alone; once eight lawful reads land, the try audit.append at 124 answers AuditFull and a granted read becomes a refusal, while refusals at 122 and 123 never reach the append. The trail's cost falls on the authorized and the quiet belongs to whoever was turned away.
think Grepping for audit outside mand/ found the second floor and it is sharper than the first. caravan/capabilities.rye:183-185 says, in its own words, that a capability system that cannot say which refusal it gave cannot audit itself -- and names Mand: "Mand's ring-1 audits on grant; a refusal deserves the same legibility." mand/capabilities.rye is a 262-line copy of caravan's 305 and publishes neither Refusal nor refusal_reason, so the sentence naming Mand sits in a file Mand copied from before it was written.
think git ls-files -s made the file mode the whole argument. Three rooms hold a capabilities.rye: caravan's original at 100644, linengrow's at 120000 -- a symlink to caravan's -- and mand's at 100644, a copy. Mand keeps the symlink habit for a different file in the same directory: mand/tally_copy.rye is 120000, pointing at ../tally/copy.rye. The tree has the tool and uses it beside the file that lacks it.
think Measured rather than asserted, so the finding could not rest on one anecdote. 140 basenames live in two or more rooms across 414 paths (220 symlinks, 194 regular files); 108 of those are held both ways somewhere, carrying 113 regular files between them. Comparing each against the implementation its siblings link: 108 byte-identical, 5 differing. Three of the five are separate modules sharing a word -- lotus/fold vs mycelium/fold, lotus/stack vs tally/stack, mikrophone/verify vs crypto/verify -- and each publishes something its namesake lacks.
think The detector fell out of the data rather than being assumed: a file publishing nothing its namesake lacks, while lacking things its namesake publishes, is behind rather than different. Two carry that signature. caravan/parse_int.rye trails tally/parse_int.rye by two comment lines with identical code. mand/capabilities.rye trails caravan's by four published items. So at this stamp exactly one file in this tree lags live code, and it is the capability table of the custody vane.
think I caught my own arithmetic before it shipped. The card first read "of 108 same-named copies, 108 are byte-identical and 5 differ," which reads as a coincidence and is a category slip -- 108 basenames carry 113 files, and 108 + 5 = 113. Verified by counting the regular files under the mixed basenames directly rather than inferring, then corrected in both the card and the essay. Earth's row is exactly about this: read the number off the thing, never off the sentence you already wrote.
obs I declined to book a REDS row, and the reasoning is worth keeping. Nothing behaves other than as witnessed -- the rings decide correctly and the copy compiles as a subset -- so this is a design finding rather than a defect against a stated contract. The repair also sits in two rooms this seat does not hold: caravan/ is parked Dream's and mand/ is unrostered. The card already carries the instrument for exactly this shape, a cross-lane find named rather than taken, and %360 set the precedent by naming its remainder and leaving it to its owners. Booking would have spent the ledger's stopping word on something that is not wrong.
obs The witness's own report line is the finding in miniature: "mand-ring1: refused path -- stranger Refused, audit unchanged -- GREEN unwelcome path." Audit unchanged is printed there as the good news, where an auditor reading that a stranger was turned away would want the second clause to be the alarm.
obs The judged half stays judged. Whether a custody trail should record refusals carries real cost on both sides -- a trail admitting refusals is one an adversary can flood deliberately, evicting the grants under a bounded ceiling. So the audit names the trade and leaves the ruling to a hand rather than proposing a patch.
obs The card had 170 bytes of room, which made a fold the price of naming the find, so I folded DIFFUSER's opening cold pass, %440's closing account, and the topology census's numbers to a shelf of my own. The rebase superseded all of it: Patchouli had shelved the same block to archive/20260906-001820_itinerary-landed-accounts.md minutes earlier, so my shelf was a third copy and I dropped it rather than landing it. What actually moved is smaller and is what the cairn now records -- two shelf pointers merged into one, three landed-account pointers merged into one, and the find seated in five lines rather than fourteen, bringing the card from 33,145 back to 32,756 under its 32,768.
obs The shelf's folded links needed repointing one level down before I dropped it, and the report card is what caught them: ../external-research/ read as construction/external-research/ from construction/archive/, so truth fell to 60 and returned to 100. A fold moves the file and keeps its text, so the text's own relative links are what the fold has to pay for -- worth keeping even though this shelf never shipped.
obs Two peers wrote to the card while this lap ran, so the send took two rebases. The second landed my day-shelf row at the BOTTOM of a newest-first table by clean auto-merge, with no conflict and nothing to resolve -- %440's lantern, fired a fourth time, in the room the card says it keeps firing in. Sorted by hand. The 20260905 count moved under me too, 56 to 58, so the pin and CHAPTERS were re-measured rather than carried.
obs Read after the rebase and worth naming against my own grades: %451, landed upstream while this lap ran, finds that measure() in prose_register_scan.sh drops every bold-led paragraph as a bullet. Two of the report card's four readings ride that classifier, and this audit leads several paragraphs in bold, so its register=88 is measured by an instrument known to skip lines. The grade stands as the standing tool reported it; a number from a patched classifier that does not exist yet would be worse than an honest one from the tool everyone else was graded by. BAKERY's seat.
loom roster=standing_equipment_cold guards=119 green=117 gated=2 red=0
